a.common('Audit a different probability claim','Read the score’s definition, keep original claims and checked outcomes separately, report assessed and unknown counts and avoid a guarantee from a small selected group.',[(12,'W1 · Interpret a matching score honestly','Use its documented feature-point meaning.'),(13,'W2 · Judge correctness from outcomes','Use the supplied reference cases and retain the unassessed case.'),(14,'W3 · Compare a claim with observed frequency','Keep the reported probability and five-of-ten result separate.'),(16,'W5 · Reject duplicated predictions as new evidence','Request actual new relevant outcomes rather than more copies of a claim.')], 'In the supplied grid, A is incorrect despite strong wording; B is correct despite caution; C is correct on its single supplied check, which does not establish calibration; D is unassessed and its 80-point match score is not a probability. There are two correct predictions among three assessed records and one unassessed. Claim types differ, so avoid ranking them as though every display were the same probability measure. Reserve Audit a different probability claim for the individual first attempt.',{13:[reference]})
